{"UserSerializer defines include_website_name without a trailing ? so serializer inclusion conventions won't treat it as a conditional include hook, causing website_name to be emitted regardless of website presence/restrictions": 0.3351941704750061, "UserSerializer serializes website_name for all viewers but it is not part of untrusted_attributes gating, exposing user's website host/path even when website itself is hidden under restrictions for TL0/anonymous users": 0.5098506808280945, "website_name compares Discourse.current_hostname directly to URI(...).host but current_hostname may include a :port suffix, causing same-domain/parent-domain detection to fail on installations running behind a non-default port": 0.2491709589958191, "On line 149, \".\" << website_host uses the << operator which mutates the string literal \".\" in place, which will raise a FrozenError if frozen_string_literal: true is ever added to this file": 0.23723793029785156, "website_name method fails to show full URL path when user's website is a subdomain of the Discourse instance's domain because the else branch only checks if Discourse host is a child of website host, never the reverse": 0.7296383380889893, "Domain matching logic incorrectly assumes all 3-part domains consist of a 1-part subdomain and 2-part root domain, breaking for 2-part TLDs like .co.uk, causing unrelated domains like example.co.uk and other.co.uk to be treated as the same domain": 0.9550185799598694, "website_name method parses website.to_s string into a URI object multiple times per execution instead of caching the parsed URI object once": 0.06518668681383133}